.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jonathan Laurence Steinberg | Founder, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 438 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $337K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["WisdomTree, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.0B market cap on $494M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $148M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 9.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 30% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.30021781470911424},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (86% sell ratio, net $4.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is WisdomTree International High Dividend ETF (DTH) a Strong ETF Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3035559/is-wisdomtree-international-high-dividend-etf-dth-a-strong-etf-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-smart_beta_etf-3035559","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795688402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":